# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The app shell must always revalidate so each deploy's freshly hashed asset
# names are picked up on a normal reload (no-cache means "revalidate before
# use", not "never store" - with etags it is a cheap 304).
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Build assets revalidate too - deliberately NOT immutable. During a deploy a
# tab still on the old index.html can request a chunk the live deployment no
# longer has; Pages answers that miss with the SPA fallback (index.html, HTTP
# 200) under this same /assets/ path. A long max-age would pin that wrong
# HTML-as-JS body for hours and the import keeps failing ("Failed to fetch
# dynamically imported module") until a hard refresh. no-cache forces a
# revalidation on every use so a bad body can never persist past one load.
# (Filenames are content-hashed, so revalidation is a 304 when unchanged.)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
